1
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Dear Zachary: A Letter to a Son About His Father is a
documentary, crime film directed by Kurt Kuenne.

2
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:24,000
In 2001, Andrew Bagby, a medical resident, is murdered not
long after breaking up with his girlfriend.

3
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Soon after, when she announces she's pregnant, one of Andrew's many close
friends, Kurt Kuenne, begins this film, a gift to the child.

4
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Self (voice), played by Kurt Kuenne.

5
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Self (archive footage), played by Andrew Bagby.

6
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Self - Father, played by David Bagby.

7
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Self - Mother, played by Kathleen Bagby.

8
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Self - Ex-Girlfriend (archive footage), played by Shirley Turner.

9
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:57,000
Self - Son (archive footage), played by Zachary Andrew Turner.

10
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Dear Zachary: A Letter to a Son About His Father is a 2008 American documentary film
written, produced, directed, edited, shot and scored by Kurt Kuenne.

11
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:15,000
It is about Kuenne's close friend Andrew Bagby, who was murdered after
ending a relationship with a woman named Shirley Jane Turner.

12
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
Turner was arrested as a suspect, and, shortly thereafter, announced she was
pregnant with Bagby's child, a boy she named Zachary Turner.

13
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:33,000
The film premiered at the Slamdance Film Festival in 2008 and received a limited
theatrical release before being acquired for distribution by MSNBC.

14
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:12,000
It received critical acclaim, particularly for its editing and emotional weight.

15
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
Kuenne donated all profits from the film to scholarships
established in the names of Andrew and Zachary Bagby.

16
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
In 2009, after watching the film Canadian MP Scott Andrews introduced Bill C-464
(also known as "Zachary's Bill") to the Parliament of Canada.

17
01:19:03,000 --> 01:19:09,000
The bill, which helps protect children in relation to bail hearings and
custody disputes, was signed into law the following year.

18
01:23:42,000 --> 01:23:48,000
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship, parent child relationship,
grandparent grandchild relationship, loss of loved one, pregnancy.

19
01:28:21,000 --> 01:28:27,000
The tone is uplifting.
